{"name":"Beyond the Sea","hex":"#005784","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beyond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Further away than.","On the far side of."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Farther along or away.","In addition; more."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beyond the Sea (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Beyond the Sea\" is the English-language version of the French song \"La Mer\" by Charles Trenet, popularized by Bobby Darin in 1959. While the French original was an ode to the sea, Jack Lawrence – who composed the English lyrics – turned it into a love song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bb/La_Mer%2C_Charles_Trenet%2C_musical_score_edited_in_France%2C_1946.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Sea_(song)","wikidata":"Q2551568"},{"title":"Beyond the Sea (Dark Moor album)","blocks":[{"text":"Beyond the Sea is the fifth full-length album by Spanish neo-classical metal band Dark Moor."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6d/Dark_Moor_beyond_the_sea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Sea_(Dark_Moor_album)","wikidata":"Q1616234"},{"title":"Beyond the Sea (2004 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Beyond the Sea is a 2004 American biographical film based on the life of singer-actor Bobby Darin. Starring in the lead role and using his own singing voice for the musical numbers, Kevin Spacey co-wrote, directed, and co-produced the film, which takes its title from Darin's song of the same title."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/BeyondSeaPos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Sea_(2004_film)","wikidata":"Q162458"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Bobby_Darin%2C_Beyond_the_Sea%2C_ATCO_record%2C_A_side%2C_1957.jpg/250px-Bobby_Darin%2C_Beyond_the_Sea%2C_ATCO_record%2C_A_side%2C_1957.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/20/Bobby_Darin%2C_Beyond_the_Sea%2C_ATCO_record%2C_A_side%2C_1957.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Bobby_Darin%2C_Beyond_the_Sea%2C_ATCO_record%2C_A_side%2C_1957.jpg/250px-Bobby_Darin%2C_Beyond_the_Sea%2C_ATCO_record%2C_A_side%2C_1957.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABobby_Darin%2C_Beyond_the_Sea%2C_ATCO_record%2C_A_side%2C_1957.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/500px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.